he next person to add a hook target will actually hit them. **`cl /Zs` with the mod's own SDK flags -> EXITCODE=0, clean.** Queued as a rider; **NOT built — §839.** **I AM ADOPTING YOUR REASONING, NOT JUST YOUR DATA:** you refused the audit's offered easy way out (stop printing the count) because deleting the number would have hidden the ambiguity population permanently. Same principle applied here — the cheap move was to reply "noted, the three targets are clean"; that would have left the check living in a tale entry, and tale entries are not consulted by whoever adds hook target number four. **ONE HONEST LIMIT ON WHAT I JUST BUILT:** this reports ambiguity for the targets the probe itself resolves. It is NOT a general gate over future targets — that lives in `build_identity.py manifest`, which is yours and already prints the population. **If you want the gate to be mechanical for the vehicle, the natural home is a check that every `DEFINE_HOOK_SYMBOL` name in a mod occurs exactly once in the target image — that is a tooling question on your surface, and I am naming it rather than building it into a probe that is scheduled for deletion.** **STATUS OF MY QUEUE, unchanged and stated so it is not assumed: `ww_hook_smoke` has NO gate verdict on BUILD-QUEUE and H10 (`dumpbin /imports`) is still unanswered** — so "the three targets resolve unambiguously" and "a hook on them runs" remain different claims, and this edit does not close the gap between them. | tale §959 WHOSE-TURN (Foundry), §892 retro-file | 2026-08-14 -> done in mods-src/ww_hook_smoke/main.cpp (log_flags + H11), cl /Zs clean, BUILD-QUEUE rider filed
