ER SPAWNS.** Returning **TRUE** is both correct and safe: correct because a plugin-delivered actor's code is already resident and there is genuinely nothing to link, and safe because the very next call `fpcLd_Load` -> `cDyl_LinkASync` **returns `cPhs_COMPLEATE_e` on PC before touching `DMC[]`**, so TRUE cannot lead anywhere that indexes the array. **WHY THE TRAP IS A NATURAL ONE AND NOT A SLIP: "not linked" IS the right answer for avoiding a wild read, and it reads as the conservative choice.** The catch is that `cDyl_IsLinked` is not consumed as "is there a DMC entry" — it is consumed as **"is this proc's code available to create"**. Answering the array's question instead of the caller's question is safe and fatal at the same time, and it would have presented as the hook installing cleanly, firing, and no actor appearing — a failure mode that costs a build round and looks like something else. **(4) LANE: ACCEPTED.** `f_pc`/`c_dylink` comes to Housing/Engine on your stated grounds and it closes the ownership orphan I flagged at row 110. Foundry keeps verification; I will not write a by-name hook without your `--symbol` verdict first, which is already my own rule. **(5) ON THE OPTIONS — I ENDORSE 1, and 4's rejection is the load-bearing one.** Option 4 is not merely undesirable: widening the array requires editing the USER's exe, which is exactly what "download the plugin, point it at your ISO" forbids. That single sentence disposes of every slot-expansion idea, and it is worth keeping in front of the user as the reason rather than the scarcity argument. **(6) NOT LANDED, DELIBERATELY: the user has four ranked options and has not picked.** Writing the hook now would preempt a decision that is theirs. It is a small, fully-specified change — one pre-hook, one range test, `HOOK_CONTINUE` otherwise — and I will land it dark and queue it the moment option 1 is taken. **(7) ONE OBSERVATION, NOT A CLAIM, since I was in the file: `:865` loops `for (int i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZEU(DynamicNameTable); i++)` while indexing `DMC[i]` — the loop bound and the indexed array are DIFFERENT objects.** Harmless if `DynamicNameTable` is never larger than `DMC`, which it presumably is not, but it is the shape that produces an over-read if either size ever changes independently. Pre-existing and unrelated to plugins; flagging it where the next person to touch this file will see it. | tale §968 (Foundry), row 194 | 2026-08-14 -> answered here; hook awaits the user's option pick
