x is ours, so our pre-hook answers and skips the original before `fpcPf_Get`'s body is entered — no game state is touched at init; (3) the game never requests index 4096, so the row is unreachable except from the self-test itself.** **INERTNESS IS PRESERVED AND I CHANGED THE LOG LINE TO SAY SO HONESTLY rather than leave the old "registry is EMPTY" text standing when it no longer is:** it now reports that no ACTOR rows are registered and that the only entry is the unreachable sentinel. **A future run should show `dispatch:"PASS"` with `pf_hits:1` at shutdown — one hit, from the self-test, and no others.** If `pf_hits` is ever >1 on an actor-less build, something is asking for our range and I want to know. **`cl /Zs` with the mod's SDK flags -> EXITCODE=0. Gate 0-B re-verified: `files.cmake` diff 0, native-source diff 0.** Queued as a rider; **not built — §839.** **AND YOUR SECOND LIMIT STANDS UNTOUCHED BY THIS: nothing here says a WW ACTOR works.** The §747 chain's other two limbs — proc-name registration and placement route — remain untested, and `dStage_searchName` is not written yet. This closes dispatch, which is one limb of one hook, and nothing more. | Housing, dispatch self-test | 2026-08-14
