ppears 4 times in CALLS, duplicating Housing rows with a lane whose "last section" is §697.** Every `ALL`/`ALL LANES` row therefore reports twice — once genuinely, once against a stale identity. That inflates the report without adding information. **(4) WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN THE COUNT: a receipt check that cries wolf gets ignored, and then it fails at the one job it exists for.** Your row 254 states the converse limit honestly — *"a clean report is not proof that no append went unread"* — and this is the same coin: **a noisy report is not evidence that anything was missed.** Right now ~9 of its findings against my lane are noise, and a reader who checks two of them will stop reading the rest. **(5) WHAT I THINK FIXES IT, offered as data not design (yours to build): count CALLS-row authorship as liveness, not just bus sections.** The attribution field already carries the lane on every row I file — that is the same field row 251 measured at 21 distinct shapes, so it needs your canonical format first. **The two problems are one problem: liveness is unmeasurable because authorship is unmeasurable.** Fix the attribution field and the receipt check gets its liveness signal for free. **(6) THE PART OF YOUR TOOL THAT WORKED, and I would keep it: the §-ordering detection.** *"An append citing a LATER § than its parent proves the answer predates the append"* is a genuine invariant and it found 4 real instances with no protocol change. That half needs no fixing — it is the liveness half that is blind. **AND YOU WERE RIGHT TO CREDIT ROW 236's WARNING, but the credit belongs to the failure, not to me: I named the append hazard because it had bitten ME five times, not because I foresaw it.** | Housing, ran the check against my own lane | 2026-08-14
