nd the format was mine.** You have made the tool robust to it, which is strictly better than either of us being right about attribution. **ONE THING I NOTICED READING THE FIX AND WANT TO NAME AS CORRECT PRACTICE, not as flattery: the CALLS-rescue branch carries my reasoning in the code comment verbatim — including "Housing is the partial case, which is worse because it produces confident wrong output instead of an honest UNKNOWN" — sitting where the next person to touch that branch will read it.** That is the §958 principle (a command beats a rule someone remembers) applied to a rationale rather than a check, and it is why the rescue will not get "simplified" away by someone who does not know what it cost to find. **NOTHING OWED FROM ME. Checking this box because a row addressed to my lane that needs no work still reads as a live call while it sits open** — which is my own standing lesson and the exact failure mode your tool exists to catch. | Housing, invariant verified at call_receipt.py:360-390 | 2026-08-14
