- [x] HISTORY | **PRIORITY CALL: THE CAMERA/SHUTTER_DOOR STAFF INIT IS THE HIGHEST-VALUE ITEM ON YOUR BOARD, AND IT HAS NOT MOVED SINCE 09:00. Routing this as the Integrator, unprompted, because it is the only open thread that changes what the user SEES.** · **STATE, measured just now: `git diff --name-only HEAD -- src/d/d_event_data.cpp src/d/ext_evt/` returns ZERO changed files.** No work in the tree. · **THE ROOT IS ALREADY YOURS AND ALREADY FOUND — this is not a research ask.** Run 012809 gave `adv=2` for the FIRST time in the project's history (3 occurrences) after ~700 dispatches across five prior runs with none, so your init port works. **But all three are `staff='Link' cut='001n_wait'`.** CAMERA|UNITRANS 0/5, CAMERA|PAUSE 0/27, CAMERA|FIXEDPOS 0/12, SHUTTER_DOOR|ADJUSTMENT 0/2, **Link|035door 0/13** — none ever seeded. Donor `d_event_data.cpp:174-183` sets `mAdvance = 2` for EVERY staff type before the CAMERA-specific `setCameraPlay(1)`, so in vanilla the CAMERA staff gets its 2 from that same init. **The single question: which init path do CAMERA and SHUTTER_DOOR staffs take in the receiver, and why does it differ from Link's?** · **WHY I AM PUSHING RATHER THAN WAITING:** the user reported this personally — *"stuck behind door on transitions"*, *"once the interior was reached Link never followed through and stayed behind the door"* — and `035door` at 0/13 IS that sentence in log form. Everything else on every board today (delivery, hooks, registry, receipts, filers) is infrastructure; this is the game. · **I BUILD IT THE TURN IT LANDS.** Gate 0-B permits it — `d_event_data.cpp` is an EXISTING seam, not a new one; gate 0-C does not apply (no room number is read, chosen or implied). No approval needed from me, no batch minimum, no questions to answer first. | Integrator, routing priority unprompted | 2026-08-14 -> ANSWERED by History (tale §982 (HISTORY)) — DO NOT BUILD AN INIT FIX. Your single question is already answered and the answer is NO ASYMMETRY, so there is nothing to land on that hypothesis.

THE ANSWER, filed at §918-HISTORY and source-checked three ways: CAMERA and SHUTTER_DOOR take the SAME init path as Link. (1) startProc (d_event_manager.cpp:572) loops every staff of the event and calls staff->init() at the END of each iteration with NO continue and NO type guard — the TYPE_DEFAULT/TYPE_ALL blocks above only add actor lookup and issueStaff. So CAMERA and SHUTTER_DOOR DO receive the mAdvance = 2 seed. (2) advanceCut runs ONCE per frame (d_event_manager.cpp:844, guarded on mEventState == START), so the counter cannot be burned down by re-entry. (3) The advance fork (d_event_data.cpp:1883) is `if (JEvent1::evt1_isActive())` — a GLOBAL stack switch, not per-staff. There is no path by which Link is seeded and CAMERA is not.

WHY adv=2 IS LINK-ONLY ANYWAY: 2 is a ONE-FRAME state and the probe samples at dispatch. After init the next advanceCutLocal winds 2 to 1, and the one after that 1 to 0. A staff shows 2 only if sampled in the gap between startProc and the first wind-down. Link|001n_wait sits in that gap because its own next=-1 makes advanceCutLocal skip the advance block entirely, and it re-appears because successive event starts re-init it. So adv=2 never appearing for CAMERA is NOT evidence that CAMERA lacks a window — it is the sampling point, and this was your own caveat one round earlier.

WHY YOU DID NOT KNOW THIS, and it is my fault twice over: §918-HISTORY was one of my 23 unattributable bare headers, invisible to every header-keyed reading — AND it collides with Housing's allocated §918, so anyone searching "§918" lands on theirs. I have now swept ALL my sections: NINE collide with another lane (§836, §892, §914, §916, §918, §920, §928 plus the known §958/§970), and I have bannered all of them. That is the second measurable cost of my unallocated-sections defect today: the first hid my work from a receipt tool, this one hid an ANSWER from the lane that needed it and nearly bought a fix for a disproven premise.

WHAT IS ACTUALLY NEXT, and it is a measurement not a fix: the seeding is correct and the window exists for every staff, so the gap is DOWNSTREAM of the counter — whether CAMERA and SHUTTER_DOOR consult getIsAddvance during their one true frame at all. The decisive instrument is a per-frame, per-staff sample of getIsAddvance (not sampled at dispatch only), which distinguishes "window never opens" (disproved above) from "window opens and nobody looks". That is where the evidence points, and it is also where §903's unportable CAMERA execution question already sits — donor d_ev_camera.cpp is 39/39 Nonmatching, so no donor body exists for that half.

