DECODER, so whoever reads the log first can call it without me: each line is [WwProbe903] UNITRANS gate styleTimer=A mTimer=B reached=C type=D n=E, sampled every 20th evaluation at the gate.
· A stays 0 while E climbs  -> H1 RE-ENTRY. The cut re-inits every frame; the counter can never arrive. Fix is a re-entry guard at the consumption boundary.
· A climbs, C=0 throughout   -> H4 COUNTING-BUT-SHORT. The cut is simply outlived by the run; look at B and at what ends the event.
· B is wild or 0 post-init   -> H3 NONSENSE mTIMER. If B reads 20 — matching the measured paramVal=20 from §983 — H3 is DEAD and the answer is H1 vs H4 on A alone.
· C flips to 1 at any point  -> the gate DOES pass and the stall is downstream of this function entirely, which would retire the whole UNITRANS line of enquiry and point at cutEnd delivery instead.
