THE MECHANISM: THE RECEIVER'S OWN INTERPOLATION COMPLETES ONE TICK BEFORE ITS OWN GATE ADMITS IT.
· The completion gate is "if (mCurCamStyleTimer >= trans->mTimer)" — needs 20.
· The interpolation on the not-yet-complete branch is (d_ev_camera.cpp:1292): my_main_f32 = (mCurCamStyleTimer + 1) / f32(trans->mTimer).
· At your measured styleTimer=19, mTimer=20 that is (19+1)/20 = EXACTLY 1.0. The camera has ARRIVED. The transition is visually finished, and the gate still says not done.
So the cut spends its final tick with the camera already in place, waiting for a counter bump it may never get. Your two numbers are precisely that boundary — 19 against 20, reached=0.

WHY THE BUMP CAN GO MISSING: mCurCamStyleTimer++ (d_camera.cpp:1471) sits INSIDE "if (dComIfGp_evmng_cameraPlay() || chkFlag(0x20000000))". The counter only advances while the event manager is still asserting camera-play. If anything withdraws cameraPlay on the frame the camera arrives, the counter freezes at mTimer-1 forever and the gate can never trip. That is a deadlock with a visible signature, and it is the user's report word for word: the camera activates and arrives, and Link never continues through the door.

WHAT I WILL NOT CLAIM, and it is the important limit: I CANNOT call the >= gate a divergence from WW. Donor uniformTransEvCamera is /* Nonmatching */ — the body does not exist in the decomp, so there is nothing to compare against. What I can say is narrower and still actionable: the receiver is INTERNALLY INCONSISTENT — one line treats (t+1)/T == 1.0 as arrival, another treats t >= T as completion, and they disagree by exactly one tick. Whether WW resolved that the same way is unknowable from source today.

TWO CANDIDATE FIXES, unranked because ranking them needs evidence I do not have: (a) make the gate agree with the interpolation — complete when mCurCamStyleTimer + 1 >= mTimer; (b) leave the gate and find who withdraws cameraPlay early, since a cut that reliably got its 20th tick would also pass. (a) is one character of intent and risks ending every UNITRANS a frame early; (b) is the honest root if the withdrawal is itself a port artifact. I would want one more probe firing — cameraPlay state on the frames around arrival — before choosing, and I am NOT asking for it now.

