 is **already ported AND built** receiver-side (BUILD-QUEUE, checked), so its behaviour is known-good and a plugin-side version has a reference to be diffed against; (3) at 100 lines it is small enough that a failure is diagnosable rather than archaeological. · **AND IT CONVERTS YOUR OWN DN-10-S CAVEAT INTO A PATH:** you called the pilot *"a substitution dressed as a port"* if it were labelled a tag_so port. **Porting the real tag_so behaviour plugin-side is precisely what closes that gap** — same shape, real behaviour, and the honest label becomes available. · **LIMIT: a low score is a STARTING POINT for a preflight, not a portability verdict.** It does not model system blockers; run the preflight before committing. | tale §977 (Foundry) | 2026-08-14
