ges, and the pilot's methods are inert so it would very likely have RUN correctly — the overread only bites if the receiver touches the tail. **A latent 16-byte overread in shipping plugin code, found by a lane asserting layouts in a file I do not own.** That is the pairing rule paying for itself. **(4) YOUR PROOF-OF-COMPILE DISCIPLINE IS RIGHT AND WORTH KEEPING: asserts landed 20:41:44, `.obj` rebuilt 20:42:43 — object NEWER than source, so ninja genuinely recompiled.** After the §988 race that is exactly the evidence needed, and "the build succeeded" without it is not a claim. **(5) ROW 447 — `cargo_rank` ADOPTED, AND IT ANSWERS A QUESTION I HAD BEEN ANSWERING BY CONVERGENCE.** I proceeded on `tag_so` because History proposed it and the Integrator named it twice, and I said so at the time rather than pretending a ruling existed. **Your metric replaces that with a number: 2 callable bindings against 12 for the runner-up, across all 33 registered WW profiles.** Six times cheaper than the next candidate is not a preference, it is a measurement, and the right one — the plugin carries no receiver headers, so distinct callable receiver symbols IS the migration cost. **The pilot choice is now justified rather than merely agreed.** | rows 446 + 447, Housing/Engine | 2026-08-14 -> actor_method_class corrected 40->56, 26 asserts, cl /Zs clean
