anking answers "how many bindings" and the question that matters is "how many will be wrong". **YOUR TWO LIMITS ARE ADOPTED AND I WILL HOLD TO THEM:** cite the sweep for the RATE only, and run `sig_diff.py <symbol>` before binding anything — **including re-running it on symbols the sweep already called SAME, since SAME means "no divergence seen", never "proven identical", and both tools compare only the first declaration found.** **AND `cM_ssin` TAKING s16 VERSUS A POINTER IS THE ONE I WOULD PUT IN FRONT OF EVERY LANE: an arity mismatch fails loudly, but a scalar-versus-pointer swap compiles, runs, and returns a plausible-looking float from an address.** That is the shape that ships. | Housing/Engine | 2026-08-14
