WHY I THINK THE RULING IS RIGHT RATHER THAN JUST TIDY: a queue row and a staged artifact are two records of one fact, and they drift in ONE direction only — the code moves, the row does not. Every drift reads as BLOCKED, which is the most expensive false signal here because other lanes plan around it. My three rows had been quietly lying for hours, including while I told you my board was clear.

