- [ ] HOUSING, FOUNDRY | **USER-ORDERED: TWO ROUTES TO WW CONTENT — a stage/room/layer warp tree, and the Fado door as the immersive one. And a finding that changes how the first gets built: THE WW DEBUG MENU IS NOT IN THE DECOMP, SO THERE IS NOTHING TO PORT.** · **THE USER'S ASK, their words: warp options *"should flow from the (possibly unported/unwired) WW byte vanilla debug menu — it has all the stages, rooms, layers… though the WW layer should sit below"* dusklight's own TP warp tree, in its own section. **Plus: _"we want the Fado door warp as part of it too — an immersive way to get there."_** · **FINDING 1 — NO DONOR SOURCE EXISTS FOR THE MENU. I looked properly rather than concluding from one filename.** The donor's `d_menu_*` set is entirely in-game menus — `cloth`, `collect`, `item`, `option`, `save`, `window`, `dmap` (188 lines, dungeon map), `fmap`/`fmap2`, `file_select`, `s_menu`. **There is no stage-select anywhere in `WW DP/src`.** That menu lived in WW's DEBUG builds; this decomp is retail GZLE01. **So "port the debug menu" is not available — and the user's own hedge ("possibly unported/unwired") turns out to be the right instinct for the wrong reason.** · **FINDING 2 — WE DO NOT NEED IT. THE TREE IS ALREADY DERIVABLE FROM THE DISC, which is MORE donor-faithful than porting a menu: 155 STAGES, 497 ROOMS, enumerated live off the FST just now via `room_layout.stage_rooms()`, WITH layout class per stage** (`sea` 50 rooms ADJACENT x283/STACKED x49/CO-LOCATED x1 · `Ojhous` NESTED x1 · `LinkRM`/`A_mori` single-room). **Layers come from the §888 selector we already ported.** Zero-bake: the tree IS the disc, read at runtime, nothing staged. · **FINDING 3 — THE RECEIVER SIDE FITS THE USER'S LAYOUT EXACTLY.** `src/dusk/ui/warp.cpp` (593 lines) already has `add_tab("Warp")`, `add_section("Destination")`, `add_section("Maps")` and a `"Region"` key — **so "WW below TP in its own section" is an add_section call, not an architecture change.** · **FINDING 4 — FADO I