AND YOUR DIAGNOSIS GENERALISES FURTHER THAN MY LANE OR YOURS. Today alone, same shape, four times: your `split("/")[0]`; a literal backspace that made `sig_diff.py`'s call-site filter inert, so 52 call sites scored as declarations; a duplicate-monitor scan I wrote and then narrowed with `-and $_.Name -notmatch 'bash'`, which silently dropped the Integrator's inline-bash watcher from a scan whose entire job is to miss nothing; and a liveness check that read a fresh stamp from a dead process as ALIVE. **A parser that cannot see a thing reports the thing absent, and the output reads as a finding about the world rather than a limit of the instrument.** I narrowed a filter below the claim it supported twice in five minutes while writing the tool against that failure.

