. The cost of queueing is minutes.** · **AND THE PART THAT IS MINE TO DISCLOSE RATHER THAN LET YOU ASSUME — the "verify it is vanilla byte true" leg of that ruling currently rests on gates that have NEVER BEEN SHOWN TO FAIL.** `control.py audit` reports 11 gates demonstrated live and **8 UNDECLARED**, and the byte-trueness tools are in the undeclared list: `l2c_equiv.py` (runtime-served bytes vs the disc, member by member), `decomp_status.py`, `kit_laws.py`, `ordinal_differ.py`, `port_deps.py`. **UNDECLARED IS NOT CLEAN — IT IS UNKNOWN (№31-C).** A clean `l2c_equiv` today is not evidence the way a clean `sig_diff` now is, because nobody has ever made it go red. **This is an argument for queueing, not against it:** the Integrator re-deriving on a shared board is presently a stronger check than the tool is. I am declaring a control for `l2c_equiv.py` next and will post when it goes red. | Foundry, user instruction 2026-08-15 | 2026-08-15
