- [ ] HOUSING | **TWO CONSTRAINTS ON THE ALIAS TABLE, BOTH MEASURED. (1) THE ALIAS MUST BE A **SECOND** `serve_file` CALL — do NOT add an `asPath` to the existing stage loop. That loop calls `serve_file(disc, i, &bytes)` with NO override, which is what mounts all 224 files under their VANILLA WW names. Change it and WW stops reading its own files. (2) There is NO alias primitive in the overlay — only `add_file`/`add_buffer`/`remove` — so a second name DUPLICATES the bytes in memory. (Integrator)** · **USER REQUIREMENT THIS ANSWERS, verbatim:** *"I do want to confirm however that for WW itself, it will still read its own files as vanilla so the game doesn't get confused with itself."* **Answer: YES, guaranteed by construction — but only if the alias ADDS a mount point rather than moving one.** · **THE PROOF, read at source not reasoned:** `serve_file` (`main.cpp:185-205`) ends in `s_overlay->add_buffer(discPath, bytes)` where `discPath` is `i_asPath` if given **else the disc's own path**. Its own comment: *"the override renames the MOUNT POINT, never the content."* **One call = one mount point. Two calls = two names, same bytes.** The stage loop at `:326` passes no override, so `/res/Stage/sea/Stage.arc` and `/res/Stage/sea/Room44.arc` are ALREADY mounted vanilla. **Add `Stg_00`/`R<NN>_00` alongside; never instead.** · **AND DO NOT COPY THE `res/Object` PRECEDENT BLINDLY — IT IS THE OPPOSITE CASE.** Those aliases exist because donor names COLLIDE with TP's own (`Always.arc`), so serving both would be wrong there. **Stage arcs are DIRECTORY-SCOPED** — `/res/Stage/sea/Stg_00` cannot collide with `/res/Stage/F_SP103/Stg_00` — **so here we WANT both names, and the object pattern would mislead you into dropping one.** · **THE MEMORY COST, flagged because the user wants this generalised to "many or all ported/wired items":** every alias re-registers the full buffer. `sea` alone has ~50 rooms; a table across many stages doubles the aliased subset of a 27.2 MiB serve. **Acceptable for the first entries, NOT obviously acceptable at scale.** · **SO A QUESTION FOR THE ESTATE RATHER THAN A BLOCKER: an `add_alias(existing_handle, new_path)` overlay primitive would make this free.** That is SDK surface — **the same shape as the `acquire_host_pane` gap already with Foundry: dusklight's SDK has no way to add a NAME to something that already exists.** Third instance of one architectural pattern. **Not designing it, not queueing it, and it does NOT block the first entries.** | Integrator, alias constraints + additive guarantee 2026-08-16 | 2026-08-16
