code comes BEFORE any receiver-side reasoning.** · **HOUSING, THE CONSTRAINT: header-free plugin.** No receiver headers, no `dStage_*`-style struct assumptions without measured offsets, and every by-name binding checked on all three legs — `--symbol` SAFE on both images, `--find` on the user's actual image for MULTI_NAME, and static-vs-member for the phantom `this`. **All three have cost a boot each in the last two days.** | Integrator, WW dialogue port assignment 2026-08-16 | 2026-08-16
- [ ] HOUSING, INTEGRATOR | **DONOR DECODE PASS 1 DELIVERED — `docs/state/ww-message-donor-spec.md`, field-by-field per the §991 precedent. IT IS HALF THE JOB AND THE HALF IT IS MISSING IS THE ONE THAT MOVES (History/Bridge).** **FILED AS A NEW ROW, NOT AS AN ANSWER TO THE ASSIGNMENT: that row is addressed HISTORY, HOUSING jointly and checking it off would silently retire Housing's implementation half.** · **WHAT IS DECODED: STRUCTURE, transcribed from donor headers with offsets** — `msg_class` **0xFC** (an fpc **leaf-draw** process, a **FIFTH profile tier**: `msg_process_profile_definition` is `leaf`-based, not `actor`-based, and it is NOT the unmirrored `actor_..._definition2` Housing flagged) · `fopMsg_prm_class` **0x1C** and `fopMsg_prm_timer` **0x34** (two prm shapes — a creator assuming one truncates the other) · `sub_mesg_class` 0xFC→0x168 · `JMessage::TControl` 0x04–0x28 and `dMesg_tControl` 0x3C–0x71 · the three processors · `dMesg_screenData_c` 0x004–0x1B0 with Talk/Item subclasses · `fopMsgM_pane_class` **0x38**. · **WHAT IS NOT DECODED, STATED AT THE TOP OF THE DOC RATHER THAN IN A FOOTNOTE: FLOW. Six `.cpp` bodies totalling 14,686 lines are UNREAD** (`f_op_msg_mng.cpp` 7637 · `d_msg.cpp` 3117 · `d_mesg.cpp` 2257 · `d_message.cpp` 1262 · `d_message_paper.cpp` 325 · `f_op_msg.cpp` 88). **A fill built from this spec will have correct field widths and wrong behaviour.** Nothing in it may be cited as *"the donor does X"* — only *"the donor stores X"*. · **TWO §991-CLASS FINDINGS ALREADY, both the kind a prose summary would have lost:** **(1) THERE ARE TWO DIFFERENT MESSAGE-CODE PACKINGS IN ONE SYSTEM.** `JMessage::TControl` packs `(groupID << 16) | messageIndex`; `fopMsgM_msgGet_c::getMesgNumber()` packs `(mGroupID << 8) | mResMsgNo` — over a **separate `mResMsgNo` field**, so there is a message number and a resource-local message number and the shift differs with them. **Pick one packing for both and every message past group 0 resolves the wrong string — and it will read as a content bug, not a field bug.** Which one the dialogue path uses needs `d_msg.cpp`; I did not guess. **(2) `fopMsgM_msgGet_c` AND `fopMsgM_itemMsgGet_c` ARE NOT LAYOUT-COMPATIBLE despite looking parallel** — `itemMsgGet_c` has **no `mGroupID`**, so its 0x08 is `mMsgNo` where the general variant holds `mGroupID`. One shape for both misreads every item message. · **AND ONE SCOPE FACT: SIX OF THE 24 STATES ARE WW-EXCLUSIVE SUBJECT MATTER** — `SCOPE_*` ×4 is the Picto Box, `TACT_e`/`DEMO_e`/`INPUT_e` are the Wind Waker conductor. The receiver has no counterpart, so `mStatus` (a **u16** at 0xF8) is a **donor-value surface**, the §843 particle-ID class, not a mappable enum. · **THE FOUR WIRES — DERIVED, NOT PICKED TO MATCH THE NUMBER.** I read what the donor refuses to run without: **W1 JMessage engine** (`dMesg_tControl` IS a `TControl` — inheritance, not preference; owns tag interpretation, which IS the dialogue feature set) · **W2 JUTFont, TWO FONTS ALWAYS** (`mMainFont` + `mRubyFont`; `setFont()` takes two; **a one-font port silently drops furigana and looks like working dialogue**) · **W3 J2D screen layer** (the box IS a `J2DScreen`; **every pane stores ORIG and live copies of position AND size — open/close is interpolation between them, so a port keeping one copy cannot animate**; `openAnime`/`closeAnime` are PURE virtual) · **W4 `fopMsg` leaf-process manager** (7,637 lines, the largest single unit; the lifecycle W1–W3 are driven by). **EXCLUDED AND SAID SO: `JKRExpHeap`** — real and load-bearing (`sub_mesg_class` owns **two**) but an *allocator*, a lifetime constraint on W4 rather than a system; **a port allocating from the host heap has changed the lifetime model, not just the allocator.** **`JPABaseEmitter`** — one screen variant's sparkle. **Overrule either; I would rather be corrected than have picked four to fit the count.** · **QUEUED, OBEYING THE QUEUE: five BUILD-QUEUE rows (parent + W1–W4), each carrying donor file:line, and EVERY ONE MARKED `BLOCKED—PASS 2` AND EXPLICITLY EXCLUDED FROM MIN-BATCH-5.** They are not buildable and I will not let them look it — that file's own warning is that a not-ready PENDING row *"distorts the count the gate runs on"*, and filing five of them silently would have done exactly that. **VERIFY on each row is `port_preflight.py` plus the Integrator's three standing legs** (`--symbol` SAFE both images · `--find` for MULTI_NAME · static-vs-member for the phantom `this`). · **OPEN, №31-C:** the `dMesg_tControl` **0x2C–0x3B gap is unaccounted** (`mRenderStack` size undeclared — **measure before mirroring, do not assume 0x3C is packed**) · `mesg_header`/`mesg_info`/`mesg_data`/`JMSMesgEntry_c` bodies untranscribed, **and that is the BMG record layout a fill actually reads** · `field_0xf0`/`field_0xf4` on `msg_class` are unnamed `u32`s sitting directly before `mStatus` — unknown, not empty. · **PASS 2 IS THE FLOW READ AND IT IS MINE.** Not urgent per the assignment — the Outset crash stays the critical path. | History/Bridge, WW dialogue donor decode 2026-08-16 | 2026-08-16
- [ ] HOUSING, INTEGRATOR, ALL LANES | **THE WW MESSAGE SYSTEM IS *NOT* VERBATIM-CLEAN — 7 OF 10 DONOR TUs ARE NONMATCHING, 93 MARKERS. I PUBLISHED A DECODE WITHOUT CHECKING THIS AND THE USER ASKED WHETHER I HAD (History/Bridge, correcting my own row).** · **MY ERROR, FIRST: I inferred "decompiled" FROM FILE SIZE.** 7,637 lines looked like a decompiled TU, so I wrote the spec on the premise that reading those bodies would yield the donor's own algorithm. **I never ran the census tools. The user asked "you checked with the census tools?" and the answer was no.** Same shape as every other vacuous pass this week: a real observation (the files exist and are large) carrying an inference it does not support. · **MEASURED NOW — `decomp_status.py`, two axes, AXES AGREE ON ALL TEN:** **MATCHED, 0 markers:** `f_op/f_op_msg.cpp` (88) · `JSystem/JMessage/control.cpp` · `JSystem/JMessage/data.cpp`. **NONMATCHING:** `JMessage/processor.cpp` (4) · `JMessage/resource.cpp` (2) · `d/d_msg.cpp` (5, 3117 lines) · `d/d_mesg.cpp` (7, 2257) · `d/d_message.cpp` (7, 1262) · `f_op/f_op_msg_mng.cpp` (13, **7637**) · **`d/d_message_paper.cpp` — 55 MARKERS IN 325 LINES**, a marker roughly every six lines; treat it as unavailable, not as source. **3 MATCHED · 7 NONMATCHING · 93 markers.** · **WHY THIS IS NOT A FOOTNOTE: THE PORT PRECEDENT IT WAS ASSIGNED AGAINST WAS VERBATIM-CLEAN AND THIS IS THE OPPOSITE CASE.** `tag_so` and `tag_kb_item` both landed as *"MATCHED 0 markers BOTH AXES (verbatim-clean per the user's gate ruling)"*. **There is no precedent in this estate for porting a NONMATCHING donor system, and whether the gate ruling admits one AT ALL is the user's call — I am flagging it, not deciding it.** If the answer is no, the four wires and the parent row need re-scoping before Housing writes anything, which is why this lands before implementation rather than after. · **WHAT SURVIVES UNCHANGED, so nobody discards the whole spec: EVERY OFFSET IN IT.** §1–§6 are transcribed from *headers*, and field layout is pinned by the ABI whether or not a function body matches. **Nothing structural is withdrawn** — `msg_class` 0xFC, the 24-state u16 at 0xF8, both prm shapes, the two message-code packings, the `msgGet_c`/`itemMsgGet_c` incompatibility all stand. · **WHAT CHANGES IS PASS 2: from "read the flow" to "read the flow, THEN VERIFY IT."** A NONMATCHING body is a **reconstruction** — it compiles to something that is not what shipped. **Citing it as "the donor's own algorithm" would be a DN-10 step-1 claim resting on the donor's PROJECT rather than the donor's BINARY**, and that distinction is the whole point of step 1. · **THE SEAM FALLS SOMEWHERE USEFUL AND SOMEWHERE BAD, and both halves matter:** **GOOD — the message-code resolution and data-entry path is mostly MATCHED** (`control.cpp` + `data.cpp` + the `f_op_msg.cpp` process shell), **which is exactly where the §4 two-packings question lives**, so that finding can be settled against citable source. **BAD — `JMessage/processor.cpp` is NONMATCHING, and the processor IS the tag interpreter: colour, pause, ruby, branch, select. So W1's engine is HALF matched and the non-matching half is the dialogue feature set itself.** The entire `d_*` message layer and the 7,637-line manager are also reconstructions. · **ON THE INSTRUMENT, because citing an undeclared gate is the error I would be repeating: `decomp_status.py` IS ON `control.py`'s UNDECLARED LIST — no negative control, so by the estate's own rule its verdicts are UNVERIFIABLE, not clean (№31-C).** Two things partly offset that and **neither is a declared control:** its `--selftest` passes **8/8** against a **1,093-TU live corpus**, and **this run produced BOTH verdicts — 3 MATCHED and 7 NONMATCHING — so the tool is demonstrably not stuck on one answer.** That is evidence, not a gate. **FOUNDRY: `decomp_status.py` already has a `--selftest`, which is the same thing you found true of `l2c_equiv` — it may be a control that only needs declaring rather than