- [ ] HOUSING, INTEGRATOR | **THE MESSAGE SCREENS ARE DECODED AND FOUR UNNAMED STRUCT FIELDS ARE NOW IDENTIFIED — THE DISC NAMES WHAT THE SOURCE LEFT OPAQUE. Also: [H4] Winditor CONSULTED and it does NOT cover this format family (History/Bridge, tale §1011).** · **13 `SCRN`/`blo1` SCREENS across `msgres` / `dmsgres` / `tmsgres`, every block walk SELF-CHECKED (declared block count vs walked) and ALL PASS.** Pane tags sit at block offset **+0x0C**, established by scoring three candidates over **122 pane blocks: +0x0C printable in 100/122, +0x10 and +0x14 in 0/122.** **THE VALIDATION THAT MATTERS IS SEMANTIC, NOT STATISTICAL — the tags read `ROOT`, `BACK`, `cur1`, `txt0`. Random bytes do not spell "ROOT".** The 22 non-printable tags are unnamed panes (J2D permits them), not decode failures. · **✅ `fopMsgM_pane_class field_0x88[4]` IS THE FOUR TEXT LINES — and THREE independent code sites already in the spec agree:** `sub_mesg_class::text[4]` · `dMesg_tControl::mLineLength[4]` · `field_0x88[4]` itself. **Four in the struct, four in the file** (`TBX1 txt0/tx01/tx02/tx03`). · **THE OPAQUE METHOD NAMES IN §5 ARE ANSWERED BY THE DISC:** `PIC1 yz00` — ***yazirushi* = ARROW** -> `arwAnimeInit()`/`arwAnime()` · `PIC1 dt00` — dot -> `dotAnimeInit()`/`dotAnime()` · and `ring_loght.bti` in the same archive -> `dMesg_screenDataItem_c::ringMove()`/`lightMove()`. **I could not have named these from source; they are only legible with the disc open.** · **THE SELECT STATES HAVE THEIR PANES TOO:** `PIC1 mc00` nesting `mc01..mc09` plus `cur1`/`cur2` cursors, with `TBX1 txc0/txc1/txc2/tec3` choice text — **that is `SELECT_2` / `SELECT_3` / `SELECT_YOKO` (§2) rendered.** · **VARIANTS, so W3 is scoped rather than guessed:** `hukidashi_05.blo` is `ROOT` + `tx80..tx83` only — **four text lines, no decoration: the minimal box.** `hukidashi_02.blo` carries **eight** TBX (`tx20…tx30`) with four arrows and two dots — a multi-region variant. `hukidashi_14_*` are PIC-only frame/decoration sets. **