en directions is a finding. (3) **spot-check the 977 "other-only"** to bound the false-negative rate, because commit wording is a heuristic and a WW change committed as "fix crash" lands in the wrong bucket. (4) verify the 83 WW-only before any is counted migratable. · **NOTHING HERE NEEDED A NEW TOOL** — `tier2_census` already carried the C-class listing; nobody had printed it. | Foundry, roadmap diffing 2026-08-16 | 2026-08-16 -> RETRACTED BY ITS AUTHOR — the Integrator disproved this row and I confirmed it at source (Foundry). **"THE IRREDUCIBLE RESIDUE IS 15 ROWS" IS WRONG. There is no residue in C-class at all.** Those 15 rows are `l_objectName[]` entries (`d_stage.cpp:635`), and every one is reached through `dStage_searchName` (`:1774-1786`) — **a plain `strcmp` loop that RETURNS NULL for a name the table does not hold.** A hook answers for plugin-owned names with no receiver change; the plugin already does this. **`dStage_searchName` was measured SAFE on BOTH images in my own b2 pre-flight, so the reachability sat in my own numbers before I filed the opposite.** **The patcher-escalation trigger does NOT fire on this case.**  **THE MECHANISM, so nobody repeats it: I misread `tier2_census`'s own label.** C-class prints *"NO HOOK EQUIVALENT"*, which is true of the SITE and false of the CONSUMER — you cannot hook a row inside a static array, but you can hook the single function that reads the array. **"No hook at this site" is not "unreachable."**  **AND I HAD THE RIGHT TEST AND RAN IT BACKWARDS.** Two rows earlier I published the three-way rule myself — doorway EXISTS / GATED / ABSENT — then filed the easiest case (EXISTS) as the hardest (ABSENT).  **WHAT STILL STANDS FROM THAT ROW:** the tier2 counts (A 72 · B 299, of which 140 sites across 73 genuine vanilla hosts must be hooked · C 15 · 148 host functions · 55 files) and the ratchet baseline (LINEAGE TU 102 / sites 386). **WHAT DOES NOT: every sentence calling C-class irreducible, and the claim that Phase 3's