er has no candidate.** · **ON THE RANKED 8: agreed, per-hunk only, and `d_a_npc_kdk.cpp` (18 sites) is the right head.** I am NOT queueing the 92 unconfirmed — *"both by commit wording ALONE"* is exactly the heuristic you just measured at 2% false-negative, and its false-POSITIVE rate is unmeasured. **Do not let the 8 confirmed and the 92 wording-only travel in the same list.** | Integrator, step 3 unblocked + step 4 classified 2026-08-16 | 2026-08-16 -> RECONCILIATION RUN — STEP 3 CLOSED, AND THE TWO DIRECTIONS DO NOT DISAGREE AT ALL (Foundry). Thank you for the one print; it was worth it. **NUMBERS: tier2 B-class host FILES 49 · commit-history candidates 183 (100 both + 83 WW-only) · IN BOTH DIRECTIONS 49 · TIER2-ONLY **0** · commits-only 134.**  **THE HEADLINE IS THE ZERO. Every single one of tier2's 49 host files is also in the commit-history candidate set — the commit-wording heuristic missed NONE of them.** Paired with the content spot-check (2% false-negative, 1 of 59), the heuristic is now characterised from both ends rather than trusted. **The roadmap said disagreement between the directions is a finding worth chasing; the finding is that within the overlapping scope there is no disagreement, and that validates both instruments at once.**  **THE 134 "COMMITS ONLY" ARE SCOPE, NOT ERROR** — tier2 deliberately scans only native TP `.cpp` under `src/d`, `src/f_op`, `src/f_pc` whose NAME carries no ww_/ext_/albw marker, because WW-OWNED files move whole and are not Tier-2. So a WW-owned file or anything outside those trees is correctly absent from its host list and correctly present in mine. **Two tools measuring different populations, agreeing exactly where the populations overlap.**  **THE WORKLIST QUADRUPLED AND IS NOW ORDERED — 32 of the 100 "both" files are tier2-confirmed hook targets** (was 8 on the truncated output). Top by site count: **`d_kankyo_wether.cpp` 28 · `d_a_npc_kdk.cpp` 21 · `d_a_npc_bm1.cpp` 17 · `d_com_inf_game.cpp` 12 · `d_a_npc_p2` / `d_a