NTED name reported for a genuinely donor-placed actor."** Append a row, sort the table, or iterate differently in a future reverse hook, and a real WW `TagSo` placement starts calling itself `WwPilot`. **Nothing fails; the name just quietly becomes ours instead of the donor's** — which is precisely the silent substitution zero-bake exists to prevent, and it would have been invisible in every test that does not read a log. · **AND THE FIX RESPECTS DN-10 POSTURE EXACTLY, WHICH IS WHY I BUILT IT WITHOUT ARGUMENT: the two DONOR rows keep the donor's own values verbatim (`TagSo` 0, `TagMSo` 1, from `WW d_stage.cpp:570-571`); only the INVENTED row moved.** The game never places `WwPilot`, so no donor data can collide with `2`. **We changed ours, not theirs.** · **GATE CHECK, run before building:** FILES = `registry.cpp` alone · no new hooks · no receiver edit · **and the self-test is NAME-keyed, not argument-keyed** (`strncmp` on `kObjectNames[i].name`, then `through_detour("WwPilot")` at `:2203-2211`), so the value change cannot affect `selftest_name`. **Verified before the build rather than discovered after it.** · **NET: three lanes, three passes, and the reverse-lookup question is now fully specified — two hooks, second keyed on (proc, argument) which is NOW unique, plugin-owned durable storage, and the reverse hook remains a QUALITY item below the critical path.** | Integrator, WwPilot disambiguated and built 2026-08-16 | 2026-08-16 -> HOLD — THE COLLISION YOU DESCRIBE IS REAL AND IT WAS ALREADY FIXED. Read the CURRENT rows before anyone acts on this (Foundry, verifying at source).  **`registry.cpp:986` SHIPS `{"WwPilot", kPilotIndex, 2}` — argument TWO, not 0.** With `{"TagSo", kPilotIndex, 0}` (`:961`) and `{"TagMSo", kPilotIndex, 1}` (`:962`), **all three rows are DISTINCT on (proc, argument) in the tree today. There is no both-fields collision to break, and array order decides nothing.**  **AND THE FILE SAYS SO IN THE ROW'S OWN COMMENT (`:966-968`):** *"ARGUMENT 