- [x] HOUSING, INTEGRATOR | **THE `encoding` FIELD IS A TRAP — BOTH BMGs DECLARE `encoding = 1` AND THEY ARE NOT THE SAME ENCODING. Group 1 is SHIFT-JIS JAPANESE left in an English build. I am also correcting a dependency I told you was required (History/Bridge, tale §1011).** · **MEASURED, not inferred:** `zel_00.bmg` — declared `encoding 1`, **1.0%** of DAT1 is high bytes (5473/533400), single-byte English. `zel_01.bmg` — declared `encoding 1`, **56.0%** high bytes (605/1080), **Shift-JIS katakana**. **Same field value, different encodings.** · **⚠ SO THE HEADER FIELD CANNOT CHOOSE A DECODER, AND A FILL THAT BRANCHES ON IT WILL MANGLE EVERY STRING IN GROUP 1.** The real discriminator is `TResourceContainer::mIsLeadByteFunc` — a predicate **set per container in code**, not a value in the file (§7.6). **I had flagged multibyte abstractly; this is the shipped instance, and it is the kind of thing that reads as "the text renderer is broken" three days later.** · **WHAT GROUP 1 ACTUALLY CONTAINS — 15 messages, `msgNo` 3401-6510, all `mTextboxType = 12`, decoded Shift-JIS:** `ヒサシブリダナ　ハイラルオウヨ` (*"it has been a long time, King of Hyrule"*) · `モシヤ　デンセツノ　トキノユウシャカ？` (*"could this be the legendary Hero of Time?"*). **LEFTOVER JAPANESE DIALOGUE IN AN ENGLISH BUILD** — archaeology, not gameplay. · **✅ AND THE CORRECTION, which is the actionable half: I TOLD YOU "a port must mount both archives to answer group 1 at all." That is mechanically true and PRACTICALLY MISLEADING.** Group 1 carries **no English gameplay text**, so mounting `bmgresh.arc` is **correctness-optional for a first port and should gate nothing.** **Left uncorrected, that sentence would have had you chasing a dependency that buys zero player-visible text.** Spec §7.10 revised in place. · **WHY I CHECKED AT ALL, since it was not on my list: I had written a requirement about group 1 without ever looking at what group 1 IS.** Fifteen entries is a two-minute read and I had asserted a mount dependency on it instead.