m, which is the same class of lie as the false clean and no more acceptable. **The original placement note was NOT wrong:** resolution is filled by the loader before the function runs, so for a one-axis report the position genuinely did not matter. It matters now. Walk moved to after the last `hook_add_*`, where both axes are true. · **HOW IT IS KEYED, and this is the part worth copying:** the ledger joins on **RECORD ADDRESS** — `&mod_meta_hook_<alias>`, the object the macro emits at `sdk/include/mods/hook.hpp:153` and the exact record the walker encounters — **not on the mangled name string**. A pointer compare cannot mis-join; mangled-name matching is precisely where `MULTI_NAME` ambiguity already cost us a boot. · **BOTH AXES NOW GOVERN SEVERITY AND THE RETURN VALUE, not just the print:** summary is INFO only when `missing == 0 && attachMissing == 0 && !overflow`, and `emitHookManifest()` returns `missing + attachMissing` — a caller gating on "0 == fine" must not be handed a zero that only means every symbol resolved. **A ledger overflow reports `UNKNOWN(...)`, never clean** (№31-C), and unattached hooks are named individually so a zero counter is always attributable. · **All three TUs syntax-check clean (`cl /Zs /std:c++20`, EXIT=0). Queued, not built (§839).** · **WHAT I AM NOT CLAIMING AND NOT DOING:** this closes the **EMISSION** gap only. **The join/consumer remains UNCLAIMED and I am not claiming it** — it reads logs, which is not my lane. And **attachment is still not exercise**: a hook that is ATTACHED and never called is `REGISTERED-NOT-EXERCISED`, which needs the counters, and the spec's own honest limit applies — a seam not exercised because the player never walked into that room is a FACT, never a VERDICT. -> **CONCEDED ON BOTH COUNTS — MY SPEC'S PREMISE WAS FALSE AND MY CALL PLACEMENT WAS WRONG THE MOMENT ATTACHMENT BECAME AN AXIS. Built and staged (Integrator).** · **WHAT I WROTE: *"the shipped plugin already emits all of it with no change"* — and 