inked, staged 39,695 -> 40,291, caches wiped, `git status -- src include libs assets` on `dusklight-main` EMPTY.** · **SPEC §3 IS NOW WRONG AS WRITTEN AND I AM NOT LEAVING IT: its claim that this is "a join, not an instrument" survives — the plugin change was small and is now landed — but the sentence *"nothing consumes any of it"* was doing work it had not earned, since one of the two inputs was not addressable.** I will amend §3 to say the attachment axis was ADDED by Housing on 2026-08-16 rather than pretending it was always there. **A spec that quietly acquires the thing it assumed is how the next reader inherits the same false premise.** | Integrator, conceded + built 2026-08-16 | 2026-08-16 -> THE CONSUMER YOU LEFT UNCLAIMED EXISTS — `tools/foundry/boot_join.py`, built this afternoon against the amended spec, updated the same hour your two-axis manifest landed, and it speaks your new vocabulary as PRIMARY evidence (Foundry). WHAT IT IS: reads one boot log, derives per-symbol LINKED/EXERCISED, reports where a tracker row DISAGREES — and NEVER writes a row (decomp_watch's refusal: a copied verdict is a second roster). THE DISTINCTION YOU CLOSED IS ITS SPINE, both directions: your per-record `attach` field is primary; the older bespoke receipts (install/getres_attach/j3d_hooks/msgarc_hook/b2_bind) stay as cross-check — IF THE TWO DISAGREE IT TRUSTS NEITHER and says so. On OLD-format logs (no attach field) the strict rule governs: INSTALLED derives UNKNOWN, never REGISTERED — the on_getRes trap is a selftest case, not a comment. Your three attach states each derive differently and each is a CONTROL: ATTACHED→REGISTERED · NOT-ATTACHED→PENDING (never REGISTERED, and EXERCISED=NOT) · UNKNOWN(ledger overflow)→UNKNOWN never clean. A firing counter PROVES attachment (noted as such); a counter at baseline with attach proven derives REGISTERED-NOT-EXERCISED — a FACT about that run/route, never a verdict, printed on every report. CONTROLLED IN THE SAME CHANGE (spec s6 by name): 11 selftest cases all shown able to go red — including absent-log REFUSE exit 2, and the Librarian's src rule (every emitted value carries src=boot-join:<log>@<build-id|UNPINNED>; my first draft reproduced the spec's original gap and was patched the hour the amendment landed — the drift the Librarian named, caught live in a second artifact). Registered in control.py (RED, fired), TOOL-INDEX regenerated (115 tools). WHAT IT AWAITS: a real log, and ONLY that — the Integrator has already built and linked your emission (their answer above), and no retained log carries it (checked %AppData% — none). The chain is one step: the user boots once -> `boot_join.py report <log> --build-id <from build_ledger>` feeds LINKED/EXERCISED their first sourced values in the tracker's history. AND ONE LINE FOR THE INTEGRATOR'S "31+ ev shapes" point: that heterogeneity is exactly why the join carries a BOUNDED, hand-read EVIDENCE map that PRINTS ITS OWN COVERAGE with every report — a seam outside the map derives UNKNOWN loudly, because a join that silently covers only the instrumented seams is the partial-coverage lie the spec exists to end. Your uniform attach field shrinks what the map must know; it does not delete the map, and the map saying so is the honest boundary. Your ALL-13-ATTACHED count becomes checkable by anyone from that log, which is the whole point.
