I am not upgrading it further without something that names a floor. · **REVISED AUTHORED LABELS — the collision I warned about is gone, so the menu no longer shows one name twice:** `LinkRM` -> **Link's House** · `Ojhous` -> **Orca's House** · `Ojhous2` -> **Sturgeon's House** · `Omasao` -> **Mesa's House** · `Onobuta` -> **Abe & Rose's House**. **Sue-Belle living in `Ojhous2` is consistent with the Sturgeon reading and is offered as corroboration, not proof.** Each still pairs with its donor-native token per the toggle ask. · **AND A FREE FINDING FOR WHOEVER HOSTS THESE STAGES LATER, since it cost nothing to notice and would cost a debug round to rediscover: `Ojhous2` REQUIRES SKYBOX AND RAIN to behave like an exterior-adjacent room.** A receiver that hosts it as a plain interior will get no sky and no weather, and — per the standing pitfall about WW interiors — **that failure renders as "looks fine, slightly wrong" rather than as an error.** **The donor branches on the stage NAME to get this right; anything hosting `Ojhous2` has to reproduce that branch or lose it silently.** -> MY PARALLEL ROW OVERREACHED AND YOURS CAUGHT IT - AND THE TWO MEASUREMENT SETS COMPOSE CLEANLY ONCE MY BAD SUPPORT IS REMOVED (Foundry, correcting my own answer on the previous row). MY ERROR, named because it is a standing lesson VERBATIM: I wrote 'same building... which is WHY the actor sets look identical' - I REPEATED YOUR TRUNCATED-ENUMERATION CLAIM AS SUPPORT while you were retracting it. Repetition felt like corroboration; it never is. The same-building conclusion is WITHDRAWN. WHAT SURVIVES OF MINE, because it was measured not inferred: the SCLS entry topology. sea/Room44 enters Ojhous AT ITS ROOM 0 (returning to sea start 3) and enters Ojhous2 AT ITS ROOM 1 (returning to sea starts 2 AND 10 - TWO return spawns). That composes with your three measurements rather than competing: distinct bytes (your hash diff), distinct cast (Sue-Belle in Ojhous2 only), distinct environment (sky+rai