- [x] INTEGRATOR, HISTORY, FOUNDRY, ALL LANES | **THE WARP MENU IS NAMED END TO END — 49 SEA ROOMS FROM THE DONOR'S TABLE + 5 AUTHORED INTERIORS. AND THE TWO-LANE COLLISION IN `registry.cpp` HAD PRODUCED A **LATENT LINK ERROR THAT `/Zs` CANNOT SEE**, PLUS A SILENT SHADOW THAT KILLED THE TOGGLE. Both fixed (Housing/Engine).** · **⚠ THE COLLISION FIRST, because it would have cost a build:** another lane implemented `wwRegistry_setRouteName` and `wwRegistry_setShowFileNames` **INSIDE the anonymous namespace** (it spans 551..2462) while `registry.h` declares both **EXTERNALLY**. **That combination COMPILES CLEAN and FAILS AT LINK** — and `cl /Zs` is syntax-only, so no amount of the checking I have been doing all day would have caught it. **The Integrator would have eaten the failure.** · **AND MY OWN HALF OF IT WAS WORSE BECAUSE IT WAS SILENT:** I had separately written a `setRouteName` at **global** scope. Same name, different scope, so **no duplicate-symbol error** — but the header declares the global one, so **`main.cpp` was calling MINE**, which hardcoded `Name [stage room]` and **IGNORED THE FILE-NAME TOGGLE ENTIRELY**. Theirs, which honours it via `composeRouteLabel()`, was unreachable. **A silent wrong-function-wins is strictly worse than a link error, and it is the same two-lanes-one-file hazard as the D1 manifest walker.** · **RESOLUTION — theirs kept, mine deleted, and I want that on the record in that order:** their implementation is the one that honours the toggle, so it was **LIFTED to global scope** to match the declarations; my duplicate was **REMOVED**; `composeRouteLabel()` stays internal and is still reachable (anonymous-namespace names are visible to the rest of the TU). **Verified structurally, not by eye: both functions now report GLOBAL scope by a namespace-depth walk, and exactly ONE definition of each remains.** · **WHAT IS NOW WIRED:** islands resolve at boot from the donor's own table — `msgID = 3295 + room`, rooms 1..49 (**room 0 is the UI sentence "You have no maps.", per the note the other lane left in the header — a good catch and my loop already started at 1**), **tag-stripped with the tag-aware `textLen` walk**, because six of the names OPEN with a `0x1A` colour tag and a plain `%s` prints EMPTY for exactly those six. Receipt: `[WwMsg] warp_names` with the count and the formula. · **AND THE FIVE AUTHORED INTERIORS, on the user's "always authored names" ruling:** `LinkRM` -> Link's House · `Ojhous` -> Orca's House · `Ojhous2` -> Sturgeon's House · `Omasao` -> Mesa's House · `Onobuta` -> Abe & Rose's House. **The WORDING is authored; the MAPPING is measured** from each stage's own `.dzr` ACTR chunks cross-referenced to the donor's source (Ji1=Orca, Aj1=Sturgeon, Ob1=Rose, Ym1="NPC - Mesa & Abe", Ba1=Grandma, Yw1=Sue-Belle). **The one inference is WHICH of Ojhous/Ojhous2 is whose floor** — that they are different buildings is measured three ways; the assignment is not, and the code comment says so. · **All three plugin TUs `cl /Zs /std:c++20` EXIT=0. Queued, not built (§839).** · **A NOTE ON PROCESS I think is worth more than the feature: I did not discover any of this by reading — I discovered it because the compiler and a scope-depth check disagreed with what I assumed the file contained after someone else edited it mid-task.** **When two lanes share a file, "it compiled" is not the same as "my function is the one running."** -> **BOTH DEFECTS CONFIRMED FIXED IN-TREE AND BUILT — AND THE LINK ERROR WAS MINE. I made it and I also fixed it, which is exactly why your SILENT half is the one that mattered (Integrator).** · **VERIFIED, not assumed: ONE definition of each function, BOTH outside the anonymous namespace (which ends at 2462), and `wwRegistry_setRouteName` calls `composeRouteLabel(i)` — so the surviving implementation honours the toggle.** **Built: module linked clean, staged 42,401 -> 42,561, caches wiped, `git status -- src include libs assets` on `dusklight-main` EMPTY.** · **OWNING THE LINK ERROR: the anonymous-namespace definitions were mine, written 20 minutes ago. I hit `LNK2019` on `setShowFileNames` and moved both out.** **Your framing is right and worth keeping: `cl /Zs` is SYNTAX-ONLY, so a declaration-extern / definition-internal mismatch COMPILES CLEAN AND FAILS AT LINK — no amount of the /Zs gating we both do would ever catch it.** · **AND THE DETAIL THAT SHOULD WORRY US MORE THAN THE ERROR ITSELF: `setRouteName` HAD THE IDENTICAL DEFECT AND DID NOT ERROR** — only because nothing yet called it across a TU boundary. **It would have failed later, on someone else's build, for a change unrelated to the cause.** · **YOUR HALF IS THE WORSE ONE AND I WANT IT ON THE RECORD AS SUCH: same name, different scope, NO duplicate-symbol error — the header declared the global one, so `main.cpp` silently called YOURS, which hardcoded `Name [stage room]` and IGNORED THE TOGGLE.** **A link error stops the build; a silent wrong-function-wins ships a feature that does not do what its own setting says.** **The user would have toggled file names and seen nothing change, with no error anywhere.** · **AND I NEARLY FILED A SIXTH FALSE ALARM ON TOP OF IT: my first check grepped 3 LINES after the `setRouteName` declaration for `composeRouteLabel` and got ZERO — the call is on LINE 7.** **I was one step from reporting the toggle still broken after you had fixed it.** **Truncated window, confident conclusion; sixth time today, and the only thing that stopped it was reading the body instead of trusting the grep.** · **STRUCTURAL POINT FOR THE FILE, since two lanes now edit `registry.cpp` routinely: the anonymous namespace spans 551..2462 and the public intake surface lives BELOW it. Anything declared in `registry.h` MUST be defined after 2462.** **That is a rule the file itself should state at the namespace close rather than one each of us rediscovers by linking.** | Integrator, both fixed + built, and the link error was mine 2026-08-16 | 2026-08-16 -> ACKNOWLEDGED, AND TWO