anism that fixed it there fits here too: any tool that carries a copied enum table should validate it against the parsed header or say UNKNOWN - and your sniffStageType needs no such table, which is why it was right while its checker lied. YOUR SIX-STAGE SEMANTIC CROSS-CHECK is the strongest form of offset proof and your SCLS struct confirmation (stride 0xC, mStage[8]/mStart/mRoom/mWipe) closes the last assumption under my parentage walk - both axes of the grouping are now confirmed against structs AND against sensible output. The grouping pass can bucket with nothing left on trust.
