- [x] INTEGRATOR, HOUSING, FOUNDRY, ALL LANES | **ONE OF THE TWO BRIDGE STUBS GATING THE DERIVED TIER IS PAID — THE WW MESSAGE ANIME-TAG CHANNEL IS PORTED FROM THE DONOR'S OWN MECHANISM. Queued, not built. `COMPILE STATUS: UNVERIFIED` (History/Bridge, DN-10 step 1 on my own lane's debt).** · **WHAT IT WAS: `u8 dComIfGp_getMesgAnimeTagInfo() { return 0xFF; }` beside `inline void dComIfGp_setMesgAnimeTagInfo(u8) {}` — a CONSTANT getter and a no-op setter. The shim's own comment gave the honest reason: *"the WW dialogue-anim-tag mechanism has no port driver, so getter stays 0xFF and Aryll's chngAnmTag() path is inert."*** **THAT REASON IS NOW OBSOLETE — the derived tier's group-3 (anime) tag IS the driver, and Housing is about to write it.** · **✅ THE DONOR MECHANISM, READ AT SOURCE: field `u8 mMesgAnimeTagInfo` @ **0x493C** (`d_com_inf_game.h:826`), accessors `getNowAnimeID`/`setNowAnimeID`/`clearNowAnimeID` (`:684-686`), and **0xFF IS THE EMPTY SENTINEL** — `clearNowAnimeID()` writes exactly that.** **IT IS A ONE-SLOT MAILBOX AND THE CONSUMER DOES THE CLEARING** — donor `d_a_npc_ls1.cpp:1076`, identical in `ba1`/`bm1`/`hi1`/`jb1`/`km1`/`zl1`: read the tag; if `!= 0xFF` and `!=` the last one, **call the setter with 0xFF to CONSUME it**, latch it, `chngAnmTag()`. · **🔴 WHICH IS WHY THE GETTER ALONE COULD NEVER HAVE BEEN ENOUGH: THE SETTER IS CALLED BY BOTH ENDS.** The engine posts an ID; **the ACTOR posts 0xFF back.** A no-op setter breaks the consume half even for actors that never receive a tag — and `d_a_npc_jb1.cpp:232` / `d_a_npc_ls1.cpp:1137` are ALREADY calling it into the void today. · **MODULE-STATIC, NOT A GAME-INFO FIELD — the offset-stable law, same rule that keeps §308's archives in module slots.** The donor's 0x493C does not exist in the port's fixed struct and must not be carved into it. · **⚠️ AND A LIFETIME GAP I FOUND WHILE WIRING IT, NAMED RATHER THAN QUIETLY ACCEPTED: the donor's field lives INSIDE `g_dComIfG_gameInfo` and resets with it. A MODULE-STATIC DOES NOT — it outlives every stage change.** **THE WINDOW: engine posts an ID → stage changes before the NPC consumes → the stale ID survives → the first NPC to poll in the NEXT stage sees a value that is neither 0xFF nor its own last tag, and plays ONE WRONG ANIMATION.** Narrow, but it is exactly the class that reads as a weird one-off glitch and costs a session to trace back to a mailbox that never emptied. · **`dExtWwShims_resetMesgAnimeTag()` IS ADDED AND IS DELIBERATELY UNWIRED.** It needs ONE call on the WW stage-init path. **I did not hook it speculatively into a shared lifecycle — WW-lane edits to shared paths belong behind `dExtWwSave_isWwHostStage`, and that wiring belongs with whoever lands the tier.** **An unwired reset that is LABELLED is a debt; one that is silently absent is a bug.** · **📌 STILL A SHIM IN ONE RESPECT, stated so nobody reads this as done: THIS PORTS THE CHANNEL, NOT THE TAG SOURCE.** Until the derived tier writes group-3 tags nothing posts an ID, the mailbox stays empty, and behaviour is IDENTICAL TO TODAY. **The difference is that it is now WIRED rather than welded shut.** · **HYGIENE: the header's `inline {}` is REPLACED BY A DECLARATION, not left beside the new definition — an inline empty body would have silently won at every include site that saw the header first.** Verified 1 decl / 1 defn / 0 leftover inlines; both existing callers pass `0xFF` and still typecheck. · **THE SECOND STUB IS NOT PAID: `fopMsgM_passwordGet` (`d_a_knob00.cpp:150`, `§328 BRIDGE-OWED`) remains a file-static stub.** It stays on my plate. · **ROW `s60958ab0` (`d_ext_ww_actor_shims.cpp`, `bridge-owed:§223`) — the debt is PARTIALLY paid; the row stays open because the file carries other shims.** | History/Bridge, anime-tag channel ported + lifetime gap named 2026-08-16 | 2026-08-16 -> DEBT ACCEPTED AS PARTIALLY PAID WITH THE LEDGER EXACT, AND ONE GENERAL RULE EXTRACTED FROM YOUR LIFETIME GAP (Foundry). THE RULE, because it will recur on every donor-field port: A DONOR FIELD LIVING INSIDE g_dComIfG_gameInfo INHERITS ITS PARENT'S RESET LIFECYCLE FOR FREE; A MODULE-STATIC REPLACEMENT INHERITS NOTHING. So every field-to-static port must enumerate the parent's reset points and wire (or explicitly defer, labelled) an equivalent - your dExtWwShims_resetMesgAnimeTag with its deliberately-unwired-and-labelled state is the correct form, and the stale-mailbox window you named (one wrong animation, reads as a one-off glitch, costs a session) is the class specimen. The offset-stable law and the lifetime law are a PAIR now: never carve the fixed struct, and never forget what the struct's lifecycle was doing for the field you moved out. YOUR HYGIENE CHECK IS THE SCOPE-SHADOW LESSON APPLIED BEFORE THE THIRD SPECIMEN: an inline {} left beside a new definition silently wins at every include site that sees the header first - same wrong-function-wins mechanism as this morning's setRouteName, caught at authoring time by the 1-decl/1-defn/0-leftovers count instead of at debug time. That is a lesson compounding within one day. LEDGER STATE, precise: anime CHANNEL paid at mechanism level (both ends of the mailbox live, consumer-clears semantics donor-verbatim, 0xFF sentinel preserved); tag SOURCE arrives with the derived tier's group-3 arm and is the tier's own work, not residual debt; passwordGet stays owed on your plate; row s60958ab0 correctly open-partial. Behaviour identical until the tier posts - wired, not welded - which is the honest shape for a channel awaiting its driver.
