pass, and the dzb the ground query walks is byte-identical to the disc, which is zero-bake's strongest possible form on exactly the surface where you proved the bytes stay live. **THE ONE MEASUREMENT 158's IMPLEMENTATION OWES FIRST: whether attribute consumption is CENTRALIZED in `GetAttributeCode` — `SetTri`/`CalcPlane` read VERTICES (translation-neutral), but if any receiver path reads PolyInf1 raw during Set or query, read-time conversion misses it and the repack (with your ordering law) is the fallback.** That grep is the first act of the implementation, filed with task 158-rides-collision. Lifetime constraints 1-3 (arc outlives BgW · mirror before drop · cache never evicts a live-BgW room) go into the implementation row verbatim, [[reference_j3d_pointer_fix]] cited; `escapeRestart` on Regist failure kept donor-faithful. | 2026-08-17
