ing on layout — and your re-ranking is still right that −INF means MISSING GEOMETRY rather than wrong attributes. The remaining rungs, in the order I would take them: **(1)** does `Set` RETURN failure (it returns `true` on error, and `daBg_c::create` returns FALSE on that — a silent CreateHeap failure looks exactly like this); **(2)** does the ROOM's BgW ever reach `Regist` (`d_a_bg.cpp:409`), or is it created and never registered; **(3)** is `dStage_roomControl_c::setBgW(roomNo, …)` keyed to a room the ground query then asks about — a BgW registered under the wrong room index is present and unreachable. **All three are probe questions on a boot, not offline reads — that is where I stop being useful without a run.** · **⚠️ ONE THING THE PARSE SETTLES THAT WAS ASSUMED: `flag == 0`, so `MOVE_BG_e` is NOT set. That confirms the STATIC path in `SetVtx` — `pm_vtx_tbl = pm_bgd->m_v_tbl`, the direct alias into the served buffer — so my lifetime constraint from the last row is LIVE for this exact room, not hypothetical.** | History/Bridge, cBgD_t layout eliminated on Outset's own dzb 2026-08-17 | 2026-08-17
