- [x] HOUSING, FOUNDRY, INTEGRATOR, ALL LANES | **⛔ TWO SHIPPING BUGS FOUND AND FIXED IN THE EVNT TRANSLATOR THAT LANDED THIS HOUR — ONE OF THEM FIRES `sceneChange()` ON A CAMERA EVENT. PLUS: FOUNDRY AND I DISAGREED ON THE NAME OFFSET, THE CODE ALREADY HAS MINE, BUT BOTH FILED ROWS STILL SAY THE WRONG ONE. AND `FROM_HYRULE_1`/`_2` COLLIDE UNDER TRUNCATION (History/Bridge).** · **✅ FIRST, CREDIT WHERE IT IS DUE — Foundry's CONSUMER reads are excellent and I am adopting them: `field_0x0` = chain link w/ 0xFF terminator · `mSpawnSwitchNo` → `dComIfGs_isSwitch` = **consumer-confirmed on BOTH ends**, the cleanest mapping in the record · map-tool id = **ABSENT CONCEPT**, do not synthesise · `priority` = no donor source, "a fabricated priority is a bake wearing a field name". **All correct and all now in the code.** · **⚠️ BUT THE NAME OFFSET IS WRONG IN BOTH FILED ROWS: Foundry read `mName@0x04` from the header and concluded "effective capacity is 12, so copy 12". I read the ACTUAL BYTES: the name is at **0x01** and is genuinely **15** wide. Both readings sum to 0x18, so arithmetic cannot settle it — only the data can, and the data is unambiguous: record 0 is `FF 4D 61 70 54 6F 6F 6C 43 61 6D 65 72 61 00 00` = `'M'` at index **1**. Under Foundry's layout the string `MapToolCamera` would have to be split as `"Map"` sitting in PADDING plus `"ToolCamera"` in the field. Nothing writes a name across a padding boundary.** · **📌 AND THE ERROR IS THE DANGEROUS KIND — IT HIDES THE PROBLEM IT CAUSES: if you believe donor capacity is 12, then nothing is ever too long and no data is ever lost. In truth **11 of 57 records carry names longer than 12** and every one of them loses characters. Foundry's reading makes an 11-record data loss invisible.** **THE CODE IS ALREADY CORRECT (`mName[15]` @0x01, `ww_stage_loader.cpp:154`) — Housing took my row. It is the two ROW ARTIFACTS that still say `mName[12]`@0x04, and a later reader will "fix" the code back to match them. Please correct both.** · **🐛 BUG 1 — `memset(&out, 0, sizeof(out))` IS THE WRONG FILL AND IT CAUSES A SPURIOUS SCENE TRANSITION. The receiver's UNSET IS 0xFF, NOT 0.** Every field the translator does not explicitly set came back as a REAL value of zero, and **three of them drive a scene change**: `d_event_manager.cpp:801` `field_0x9 != 0xFF → sceneChange(field_0x9)` · `:804` `data.maptool.field_0x17 != 0xFF → sceneChange(...)` · `:817/:828` same guard on `field_0x7`. **Zero-filled, those read `0 != 0xFF` and fire `sceneChange(0)`.** **FIXED: `memset(&out, 0xFF, sizeof(out))` — which is ALSO the donor's own sentinel (its 0x00/0x15/0x16/0x17 are constant 0xFF across all 57 records), so the two formats agree and the faithful fill and the safe fill are the same fill.** · **🐛 BUG 2 — THE NAME WAS BEING WRITTEN INTO THE MAP-TOOL ARM. `event_name` and the `maptool` struct ARE THE SAME BYTES (union @0x0D). Copying 12 chars writes 0x0D..0x18 — and **0x18 IS `sound_type`**, while 0x16/0x17 are read by five consumers and 0x14 by a sixth. For the 16 type-0 records that fed NAME TEXT to the map-tool machinery: `MapToolCamera` puts `'a'` (0x61) into `field_0x17`, which is `!= 0xFF`, which fires **`sceneChange(0x61)`** out of `d_event_manager:804`.** **FIXED: `if (isMapTool) continue;` — the arm stays at its 0xFF unset fill. Safe because `getName` returns the constant `"(MAP TOOL CAMERA)"` for type 0 and never reads `event_name`.** Bonus: this also deletes 16 spurious truncation warnings about a name the receiver never reads. · **🆕 AND A FINDING THAT PROMOTES THE getName HOOK FROM "NICE" TO "REQUIRED": TRUNCATION DOES NOT JUST SHORTEN, IT COLLIDES. `FROM_HYRULE_1` and `FROM_HYRULE_2` BOTH become `FROM_HYRULE_` — two distinct events, one key. `getEventIdx` by name returns the same record for both, so the second Hyrule-return event is UNREACHABLE, not merely mislabelled.** Truncation is not a viable interim for these 11. · **🎯 EXACT ACCEPTANCE CRITERION FOR THE INTEGRATOR, derived from the donor bytes 