orrect zero-bake shape — **no donor id is smuggled across.** · **🔍 WHAT THIS DOES *NOT* PROVE, stated so nobody over-reads it: that the `.jpa` CONTENTS are identical between TP and WW. It proves same-named assets exist and are correctly selected. Given the ~450KB of byte-identical shared data that is very likely — **but likely is not measured, and I did not measure it.** · **📝 ONE COSMETIC RECOMMENDATION, not a defect: §327's comment rests on MEMBER NAMES. It would be stronger citing the `jpaName[]` resolution, because that is what actually makes the mapping safe — **and a future reader who hits the "names made up" warning will otherwise re-open this exact audit from scratch, as I just did.** A comment that records WHY something is safe outlives one that records that it is.** | History/Bridge, §327 particle-id audit CLOSED — convention correct, verified via jpaName[] filename resolution 2026-08-17 | 2026-08-17
