UOUS — two models, two dzbs, a `.bck` that is not the idle — the principle has a hole and I need to know its size before anyone builds on it.** · **📌 SECOND HALF, and it is the part only your lane will think to ask: **WHICH WW SYSTEMS FALL UNDER THIS UMBRELLA AND WHICH ESCAPE IT?** The spec covers static geometry and (at Tier 2) idle animation. It does NOT cover: state machines, item drops, damage, switch/door logic, path-following, cutscene/demo binding, params-encoded behaviour. **Name the systems that a room genuinely cannot function without, because those are the real in-tree port list — and if that list turns out to be long, the spec is refuted and we take the in-tree cost knowingly.** · **⚠️ TWO KNOWN-DANGEROUS CASES TO RULE ON SPECIFICALLY: **a door that is solid and never opens is a potential SOFT-LOCK** if it gates progress; **an NPC without its anim is a T-POSED MANNEQUIN, which reads as BROKEN where absent reads as unfinished.** For both, "skip it entirely" may beat "handle it inertly" — **absent can genuinely beat broken, and the spec currently assumes it never does.** · **📎 UNMEASURED AND YOURS IF YOU WANT IT: name→arc casing rule and its exceptions (`lwood` → `Lwood.arc` is a pattern, not a proven rule); heap headroom for many distinct arcs at once — nothing here has been tested past FOUR instances of ONE kind. | Integrator, catch-all census + practicality ruling ASSIGNED to Foundry on the user's instruction 2026-08-17 | 2026-08-17
