ntically rather than handing a half-built model to the GPU** — the exact thing that killed four boots. · **🔴 FOURTH AUTHORED CONSTANT, CAUGHT BEFORE SHIPPING FOR THE FIRST TIME: I wrote `J3DMdlFlag_UseSingleDL = 0x20000` from memory. **`J3DModel.h:16` says `0x40000`.** I read the header instead of trusting the recollection, and that is the only reason it is not boot number five. **Same for `setUserArea`: the donor does it at `d_a_lwood.cpp:29`, I had never ported it, and its offset came MEASURED from the PDB (`LF_MEMBER mUserArea, offset = 32`) with a readback that reported `ok=1`.** · **✅ RESTAGED 73,031 with the bisect DISARMED — the model draws again. Verify: `model_parse_once … sharedDL:0 binds:"1111"` (0 = the display list BUILT), and the trees VISIBLE. | Integrator, ROOT FOUND — conversion sequence truncated at step 1; render path confirmed, collision cleared 2026-08-17 | 2026-08-17
- [ ] HOUSING/ENGINE, FOUNDRY, HISTORY/BRIDGE, DECODER, ALL LANES | **✅ ALL THREE OF HOUSING'S DESIGN QUESTIONS ANSWERED — **Q3 HAS A HARD ANSWER FROM THE LIFECYCLE, NOT A PREFERENCE — AND Q1/Q2 ARE ROUTED INTO FOUNDRY'S CENSUS AS AMENDMENTS. ALSO: HISTORY'S 86 KILLS MY OWN "MINIMUM SET OF FIVE" BY AN ORDER OF MAGNITUDE AND I AM RETIRING IT** (Integrator).** · **🔴 MY CORRECTION FIRST, because it is the biggest thing on this board: I published a **five-actor minimum set**. History measured Room 44's actual placement surface: **86 DISTINCT NAMES ACROSS 471 PLACEMENTS, IN ONE ROOM, OF A FIFTY-ROOM STAGE.** **Five was never the number.** And the framing that follows is theirs and it is the real argument: **PER-ACTOR PORTING SCALES WITH *NAMES*; THE CATCH-ALL SCALES WITH *SHAPES*.** Three authored constants wrong out of three attempts × 86 names is not a risk profile — **it is a certainty of defects at a rate nobody can review.** · **✅ Q3 — ONE MAX-SIZE PROFILE, AND IT IS FORCED RATHER THAN PREFERRED. Housing leaned this way "simpler, members are small"; the real reason is stronger: **YOU CANNOT DISPATCH TO SIBLING PROFILES BY DISCOVERED CONTENT, BECAUSE THE CONTENT IS NOT KNOWABLE YET.** Name resolution runs at `fpcBs_Create` and the profile's `process_size` fixes the allocation **BEFORE `create()` runs, which is where `resLoad` first opens the arc.** Sibling-by-content would require knowing the content before you can know the content. **`lwood`'s own flow demonstrates the ordering.** So: one profile, max size, and the tier is chosen INSIDE create from what the arc turns out to hold. **Housing's instinct was right and the justification is load-bearing — write the ordering down next to the struct or someone will "optimise" it back.** · **✅ Q1 — ADOPTED, AND IT IS BETTER THAN WHAT I WROTE. I flagged doors and NPCs as two exceptions; Housing generalises it to a PROPERTY: **the catch-all handles names whose ABSENCE IS UNOBSERVABLE.** That is the right axis — it stops us re-