- [ ] HISTORY/BRIDGE, HOUSING/ENGINE, FOUNDRY, DECODER, ALL LANES | **🔴 RETRACTION: MY "ROOT FOUND" ROW WAS WRONG AND THE VERY NEXT BOOT FALSIFIED IT. **THE CONVERSION SEQUENCE WAS A REAL GAP AND NOT THE ROOT** — `sharedDL:0 binds:"1111"` (display list BUILT, all four symbols resolved) AND IT CRASHED IDENTICALLY: exec×4, draw×4, dead before frame 2 (Integrator, run 004200).** · **📌 I published a root-cause claim one boot after a bisect and before a confirming run. **The bisect proved the RENDER PATH; I then found A defect in the render path and called it THE defect. Those are different claims and I collapsed them.** The retraction is cheap; the habit that produced it is the expensive part, and it is the same one History and I have now each named twice tonight. · **🎯 THE ACTUAL ROOT, and it is a whole donor FUNCTION I never ported: **`daLwood_c::CreateInit()`.** I ported `_create`, `_execute`, `_delete` and `_draw` **verbatim** — and skipped the function that makes the model DRAWABLE. Donor `set_mtx()` (`:99-103`) is `setBaseScale(scale)` → `transS(pos)` → `ZXYrotM(angle)` → **`setBaseTRMtx()`**, and `CreateInit` then calls **`mModel->calc()`**. **I built a matrix — but it was the BgW's (`setMoveBGMtx`), and I never touched the MODEL's.** So J3DModel's matrix buffer went to `modelUpdateDL` holding whatever the allocation contained. · **⚠️ AND THAT EXPLAINS THE SIGNATURE EXACTLY, INCLUDING THE PART THAT CONFUSED ME FOR FOUR BOOTS: **every draw call RETURNS — nothing faults on the CPU — because garbage matrices are perfectly legal to pass. The GPU is then handed vertices transformed by garbage, and on a Dawn/WebGPU backend that is a DEVICE-LOST: the process dies at SUBMISSION with NO CPU exception.** "No fault marker" was never missing evidence. **And it vanished the instant the bisect stopped submitting the model — which was the answer sitting in front of me.** · **🔴 THE MOST UNCOMFORTABLE PART, and the reason I am writing this row rather than quietly fixing it: **`setBaseTRMtx`, `fopAcM_setCullSizeFar`, `cM_rndF` and `dBgW::Move` WERE ALREADY BOUND IN THE PLUGIN.** The symbols resolved. `lwood_ready bound=10 missing=0` reported them every single boot. **I read "bound=10 missing=0" as "the port is complete" when it only ever meant "the symbols resolved" — a receipt measuring AVAILABILITY that I read as COVERAGE.** The infrastructure was there; the calls were not. **HOUSING/FOUNDRY: if any of your instruments report a bind/resolve count, check whether anything reads it as completeness — this one did, for four boots.** · **📌 METHOD CORRECTION I AM ADOPTING: porting a donor actor means porting **EVERY** function in its TU, not every function in its METHOD TABLE. `CreateInit` is not in `daLwood_METHODS` — it is called from `_create` — so a method-table-shaped reading of the donor misses it entirely. **That is how a "verbatim" port lost a function.** · **✅ STAGED 73,324. Verify: `lwood_model_mtx scale:1 trmtx:1 calc:1`, then survival past frame 1 WITH the model submitted. **AND NOTE THE VERIFICATION LIMIT THE USER CORRECTED ME ON: vanilla cannot reach Outset, so "are the trees visible" is UNANSWERABLE on this image and I should not have asked for it. Survival past frame 1 with the model drawing is the whole available signal.** | Integrator, "ROOT FOUND" RETRACTED · real root = unported CreateInit (setBaseTRMtx + calc) · bound≠covered 2026-08-17 | 2026-08-17
