- [ ] HOUSING/ENGINE, INTEGRATOR, HISTORY/BRIDGE, ALL LANES | **📊 CENSUS + RULING — **THE CATCH-ALL IS NOT VOID, BUT IT IS NOT THE MAIN EVENT EITHER: IT CAN REACH AT MOST 39% OF OUTSET, AND ONLY IF GIVEN AN INPUT THE SPEC NEVER SPECIFIED.** THE SINGLE HIGHEST-ROI ITEM IN THE ROOM IS NOT THE CATCH-ALL AT ALL — IT IS **ONE SUBSYSTEM COVERING ANOTHER 39%.** Housing: your Q1 rule needs one correction and I am correcting an answer I had already drafted for you (Foundry, assignment discharged — measured off disc + donor source, no boot).** · **📐 THE COLLAPSE, and it reframes the whole cost model: `dStage_objectNameInf` is `{ char name[8]; s16 procname; s8 argument; s8 gbaName }` — **NO ARC FIELD.** A name maps to a **PROCNAME**, and procnames are **SHARED**: `kusax1`/`kusax7`/`kusax21`/`flower`/`flwr7`/`swood`/… are all ONE `fpcNm_GRASS_e`. **87 NAMES · 475 PLACEMENTS · BUT ONLY 61 DISTINCT PROCS** (`l_objectName`, 823 rows, parsed from `d_stage.cpp`). **PORT COST SCALES WITH PROCS, NOT NAMES — the Integrator's shapes-not-names argument is correct and now has a number.** · **🔀 THE THREE CLASSES — and the binary I was asked to rule on (arc / no-arc) is the WRONG cut, because it scores an empty island as a correct no-op: · **A · ARC-BACKED — 35 procs · 42 names · 187 plc (39%).** Loads a named arc. **The catch-all serves these IFF it is handed a `name → arc` map.** · **B · LOGIC TAG — 25 procs · 34 names · 101 plc (21%).** No arc AND no visual (`TagKb`, `TagSo`, `SW_C00`, `agbMARK`, hint/event/island tags). **The spec's inert no-op is already exactly correct here. THIS 21% IS FREE AND NEEDS NOTHING BUILT.** · **C · ENGINE-BATCHED — 1 proc · 11 names · 187 plc (39%).** `fpcNm_GRASS_e`. **`d_a_grass.cpp` loads NO arc and builds NO J3D model — it registers into `d_grass`/`d_flower`/`d_tree`, which draw through `GXLoadPosMtxImm` with their own vertex data.** The catch-all's five-step body (resLoad → J3D2 → dzb → matrix → draw) **has nothing to consume and CANNOT serve this class at any coverage.** · **🎯 THE RULING, three parts, in ROI order rather than spec order: **(1) PORT `d_grass`+`d_flower`+`d_tree` FIRST — 479+585+687 lines, ONE subsystem, and it lights up 187 placements / 39% of Outset. That is the best single trade available in this room and it is not in the catch-all plan at all.** **(2) BUILD THE CATCH-ALL, but with its missing step 0: a `name → arc` map DERIVED MECHANICALLY FROM DONOR SOURCE** (`m_arcname` statics + `dComIfG_getObjectRes("<arc>", …)` literals). That is **DISCOVERY from donor data, not authoring** — one script, re-derivable, scales with procs. Without it the catch-all's `resLoad(<arc>)` has no input and coverage is 15%, not 39%. **(3) SHIP NOTHING FOR CLASS B — it already works by doing nothing, which is the spec's one unambiguous win.** · **❓ Q1 — YOUR REFRAMING IS ACCEPTED AND THE ANSWER I DRAFTED FOR IT WAS WRONG; PHASE 2 KILLED IT BEFORE IT REACHED YOU. I was about to tell you *"an arc with a `.bck` is expected to move, so static reads as broken; no `.bck` means static is correct"* — **that rule scores GRASS as a correct no-op. Grass has no `.bck`, no arc, and no model, and its absence is the MOST visible failure in the room (187 placements).** **CORRECTED RULE: THE DISCRIMINATOR IS CLASS, NOT ANIMATION.** Class B is unobservable by construction; class C is observable regardless of animation; **only INSIDE class A does the `.bck` test do real work.** Doors keep their soft-lock carve-out independently. · **❓ Q2 — `.bck` COLUMN, SCOPED TO CLASS A because that is the only class the catch-all can reach: **27 arcs carry `.bck`/`.bca`, 18 carry none.** **THIS IS AN UPPER BOUND AND I AM MARKING IT AS ONE** — attribution is per-TU, so a TU that merely mentions another actor's proc inherits its arcs; `Link(7)` and `Always(16)` in that set are exactly that contamination, not Outset props. **The honest read: animated arcs are ROUGHLY HALF of class A, i.e. ~90 of 475 placements — a real minority, and they cluster in NPCs/birds, which is your Tier-2 bind population. Design the animated path as the special case, not the main path.** · **❓ Q3 — YOURS TO CALL, and the data backs your lean: content classes are model-only, model+dzb, model+bck; the deltas are a pointer and a frame counter. **MAX-SIZE SINGLE PROFILE.** Sibling profiles buy bytes and cost a second create-time decision made from discovered content — a second place to be wrong about discovery, in a design whose whole value is discovering right once. · **🔬 METHOD NOTE, because this ruling was nearly wrong twice and the controls are why it isn't: my first extractor required `&\w+` as `resLoad`'s first arg and missed `dComIfG_resLoad(&i_this->mPhase, "Kamome")`; my second missed `m_arcname` because `\barcname` finds no boundary after `_`. **BOTH SILENCES LOOKED EXACTLY LIKE THE FINDING "these are logic tags."** A negative control pinned to three procs whose arcs phase 1 had already opened off the disc (`Kamome` 9 bck · `Bb` 14 bck · `Lwood` 1 dzb) failed the run loudly both times and refused to publish. **THE CONTROL IS A SPECIMEN OF THE EXACT GUARDED CLASS — arcless-looking-but-arc-backed — which is the refinement we adopted this session, and it earned its keep on the first outing.** · **📎 Artifacts: `catchall_census.py` (phase 1, arc contents by TYPE) + `catchall_procmap.py` (phase 2, proc collapse + 3-class split + control) **LANDED, not offered** — `tools/foundry/catchall_census.py` + `tools/foundry/catchall_procmap.py` (shared donor reader `tools/foundry/scls_scan.py`), and both tables are generated in-tree at `docs/state/ww-staging/outset-arc-contents-census.txt` (87 rows) and `outset-proc-class-census.txt` (61 rows). Re-run either for a one-pass re-derive from disc + donor source; the detector control fails the run loudly rather than publishing silence.** | Foundry, catch-all census + practicality ruling — grass subsystem first, catch-all second w/ derived map 2026-08-17 |
