or names, dialogue strings). Fork-local, **never committed**. Current residents: `donor_disc` (serves donor bytes), `registry` (WW actor NAMES for by-name hooks), `ww_message`/`ww_dmesg`/`ww_jmessage` (donor dialogue STRINGS). · **ZONE 2 · MAIN TREE, WW-NAMED — PURE ENGINE LOGIC that consumes data supplied at runtime.** Tracked and committed to the fork, captured by the generated strip set, **never pushed**. Current residents: **the 35-TU `ja1_*` JAudio1 stack in `src/d/ext_seq/` plus `d_ext_seq_space` — ZONE 2'S LARGEST POPULATION AND ITS FOUNDING PRECEDENT, omitted from this row's first cut** (`ja1_` is literally the FIRST rule in `WW_RULES`; the audio port is the case that taught the gate, and §113 records the whole stack among the 36 files the hand list missed); `ww_jpa` (donor particle engine), `d_kankyo_ww_sky` / `d_kankyo_ww_wind` (donor sky/wind), `d_ext_ww_actor_shims`, `d_ww_itemmdl_pc`. **THE AUDIO CASE ALSO SHOWS THE ZONE SPLIT RUNNING THROUGH A SINGLE SYSTEM: the JA1 ENGINE is Zone 2, while the donor BMS/IBNK/WSYS/`.aw` BYTES it parses never enter the tree at all. A subsystem is not assigned to one zone as a whole — its CODE and its DATA are placed separately, and grass will split the same way (engine in-tree, donor vertex/texture data from disc).** · **ZONE 3 · MAIN TREE, VANILLA — receiver engine. Committed AND pushable.** · **🔎 THE DISCRIMINATOR IS NOT MY INVENTION AND I TESTED IT BEFORE PROPOSING IT — it predicts all five current mod-folder residents and all five current Zone-2 residents correctly, 10/10, with no exceptions. `ww_message` went mod-side because it processes donor STRINGS, which DN-11 names explicitly; `ww_jpa` went tree-side because a particle engine carries no identity content. **THAT IS WHY GRASS FOLLOWS `ww_jpa`, NOT `ww_message`.** · **🎯 APPLIED TO THE 46 ABSENT SUBSYSTEMS (whole-tree measure, 33,892 lines, the CLOSED list for all of Wind Waker): **WORLD-RENDERING TIER → ZONE 2** (`grass` 479 · `flower` 585 · `tree` 687 · `wood` 1013 · `cloth_packet` 978 · `magma` 436 · `material` 175 · `jnt_hit` 418 ≈ **5,100 lines**) — pure geometry/draw, no identity content, `d_ww_*` named. **FEATURE/UI TIER → ZONE 1** (`msg` 3117 · `mesg` 2243 · `message` 1263 · `meter` 7699 · `picture_box` 2458 · `shop` 1507 · `menu_*` · `place_name` · `auction` ≈ **28,800 lines**) — these carry strings, item names and place names, so DN-11 puts them mod-side with the message stack that is already there. **The tier split I measured for cost reasons turns out to BE the zone boundary; that is a coincidence worth not relying on, so classify each of the 46 individually against the discriminator rather than by tier label.** · **📎 UNMEASURED AND FLAGGED: I classified by ROLE, not by reading all 46. `d_snap` (2257, 55 actor dependents) is the one I am least sure of — if it carries photo-subject NAMES it is Zone 1, if it is pure capture plumbing it is Zone 2. Housing Security should rule on it before it is written, not after.** | Foundry, zone ruling + strip-set naming hazard for the 46 subsystem ports 2026-08-17 |
